window.CHINA3={"generated":"2026-11-07","sources":{"meta":{"project":"China3 — Getting CNY out of China as a US citizen","checked":"2026-11-07","tiers":{"official":"Government, regulator, statute, treaty text or official gazette published by the issuing authority.","official-secondary":"Official guidance, Q&A, operation manual or consolidated index published by the same authority.","third-party":"Non-government reproduction or commentary. Used only where no official URL could be reached; always flagged for review."}},"sources":[{"id":"S01","title":"个人外汇管理办法 (Measures for the Administration of Individual Foreign Exchange)","publisher":"People's Bank of China — Order [2006] No. 3","url":"https://www.safe.gov.cn/safe/2006/1225/5319.html","tier":"official","checked":"2026-11-07","supports":"Legal definitions of 境内个人 (PRC-ID-holding Chinese citizens) vs 境外个人 (foreign passport holders) in Art. 37; annual-total framework in Art. 9; prohibition on splitting quotas in Art. 7; Art. 13 (non-resident's China current-account RMB income may be converted and remitted); Art. 14 (unused inbound FX returned by原路); Art. 15 (re-conversion of unused RMB); Art. 20 (gifts/transfers abroad by residents need SAFE approval); Art. 22 (non-resident's proceeds from selling China property may be converted and remitted with SAFE approval); Art. 26 (individual property outward transfer governed by the separate 2004 measures)."},{"id":"S02","title":"个人外汇管理办法实施细则 (Implementing Rules), 汇发[2007]1号","publisher":"State Administration of Foreign Exchange (SAFE)","url":"https://www.safe.gov.cn/safe/2007/0105/5320.html","tier":"official","checked":"2026-11-07","supports":"USD 50,000 per-person annual total for 结汇 and for 境内个人购汇 (Art. 2); above-quota current-account purchase with genuine documents (Art. 12); 境外个人 conversion of lawful current-account RMB income and 24-month re-conversion window with the original exchange memo (Art. 13); 境外个人 outward remittance from an FX savings account on ID alone (Art. 15); QDII access by residents (Art. 17); emigrant/inheritance transfer referred to the 2004 Measures (Art. 20); cash withdrawal above USD 10,000 requires prior SAFE filing (Art. 30); cash deposit above USD 5,000 (Art. 31). Page carries a note that Art. 39 was repealed by 汇发[2023]8号."},{"id":"S03","title":"个人财产对外转移售付汇管理暂行办法 (Measures on the Sale and Payment of Foreign Exchange for Outward Transfer of Individual Property), PBC Announcement [2004] No. 16","publisher":"People's Bank of China, published on the SAFE portal","url":"https://www.safe.gov.cn/safe/2004/1116/5461.html","tier":"official","checked":"2026-11-07","supports":"Only two categories exist — 移民转移 (emigrant transfer) and 继承转移 (inheritance transfer) — Art. 2; property must have been owned before emigration status was obtained; must be applied for once for the whole amount and remitted in stages (≤50%, then ≤50% of remainder after 1 year, balance after 2 years), with one-off remittance if total ≤ RMB 200,000 — Art. 6; required documents including 户籍注销证明 (cancelled PRC household registration) and embassy-issued/authenticated proof of settlement abroad, plus a tax certificate from the tax authority — Art. 8; approval by the local SAFE branch up to RMB 500,000 and by SAFE headquarters above that — Art. 10; bank must wire directly to the applicant's own account abroad and may not pay cash — Art. 11; false documents punished under Art. 40 of the FX Regulations — Art. 13."},{"id":"S04","title":"个人财产对外转移业务问答 (Q&A on outward transfer of individual property)","publisher":"SAFE Anhui branch","url":"https://www.safe.gov.cn/anhui/file/file/20170728/c662967c1ff746b9805002873a2150f0.pdf","tier":"official-secondary","checked":"2026-11-07","supports":"Q1: other forms of individual property transfer fall outside these measures; Q5: a person who has only just received an immigrant visa cannot apply — the applicant must already hold foreign permanent residence or foreign (or HK/Macau/Taiwan) citizenship; Q12: no cash withdrawal — funds must be wired to the applicant's own account; Q13: the whole amount must be applied for in one application (remittance may be split); Q15/16: a tax certificate is required, but not where the total property transferred is below RMB 150,000; lists the further instruments relied on (汇发[2004]118号, 国税发[2005]13号, 汇发[2009]9号, 汇发[2009]21号, 汇发[2014]2号)."},{"id":"S05","title":"中华人民共和国外汇管理条例 (Foreign Exchange Administration Regulations), State Council Order No. 532","publisher":"State Council of the PRC — gov.cn","url":"https://www.gov.cn/zhengce/2008-08/06/content_2602514.htm","tier":"official","checked":"2026-11-07","supports":"Art. 5 (no restriction on current international payments and transfers); Art. 12 (genuine, lawful transaction basis required); Art. 17 (outbound direct investment / portfolio transactions by residents require registration); Art. 22 (capital-account payments require approval where prescribed); penalties — Art. 39 evasion of exchange control (≤30%, or 30%–100% if serious), Art. 40 illegal arbitrage of FX, Art. 41 inbound violations, Art. 42 illegal carriage of FX across the border (warning, ≤20%), Art. 45 private/unlawful FX trading (warning, confiscation, ≤30%, or 30%–100% if serious), Art. 48 false documents / failure to declare (individuals ≤ RMB 50,000); Art. 52 definitions, including 境内个人 covering foreigners residing continuously in China for one year or more."},{"id":"S06","title":"外汇局就规范银行卡境外大额提取现金交易有关问题答记者问 (SAFE Q&A on 汇发[2017]29号, overseas card cash withdrawals)","publisher":"SAFE, republished by gov.cn","url":"https://www.gov.cn/zhengce/2017-12/31/content_5251958.htm","tier":"official","checked":"2026-11-07","supports":"Overseas ATM cash withdrawals on domestic cards are capped at an aggregate of RMB 100,000 equivalent per natural person per calendar year (all cards and supplementary cards combined) and RMB 10,000 equivalent per card per day; exceeding the annual cap suspends overseas cash withdrawals for the current and following year and may be penalised under the FX Regulations; card spending abroad for genuine current-account purposes does not count against the USD 50,000 facilitation quota; borrowing or lending cards to evade the cap is prohibited."},{"id":"S07","title":"个人外汇管理业务操作指南 (2019年版) — individual FX business operations guide","publisher":"SAFE Jilin branch","url":"https://www.safe.gov.cn/jilin/file/file/20190617/f092dca0704e4111b972e2fa14c3e1ae.pdf","tier":"official-secondary","checked":"2026-11-07","supports":"Export travellers may in principle not carry more than USD 10,000 equivalent in foreign cash; above that a 携带外汇出境许可证 must be obtained from SAFE and only in the special situations listed; cites 汇发[2003]102号 and 汇发[2004]21号 as the governing rules."},{"id":"S08","title":"关于进一步防范和处置虚拟货币等相关风险的通知, 银发〔2026〕42号","publisher":"People's Bank of China and seven other ministries","url":"https://www.pbc.gov.cn/tiaofasi/144941/3581332/2026020619591971323/index.html","tier":"official","checked":"2026-11-07","supports":"Virtual currency has no legal-tender status; RMB-to-virtual-currency conversion and related business are illegal financial activities and strictly prohibited; financial institutions may not provide account, transfer or settlement services for such activity; investing in virtual currency or RWA tokens contrary to public order is void and losses fall on the investor; this notice replaced 银发〔2021〕237号 with effect from 6 February 2026."},{"id":"S09","title":"中华人民共和国个人所得税法 (Individual Income Tax Law of the PRC, as amended 2018)","publisher":"State Taxation Administration","url":"https://www.chinatax.gov.cn/n810219/n810744/n3752930/n3752974/c3970366/content.html","tier":"official","checked":"2026-11-07","supports":"Art. 1 (resident = domiciled, or 183+ days in a tax year; non-residents taxed only on China-source income); Art. 2 closed list of nine taxable income categories — currency conversion is not one of them; Art. 3 rates (3%–45% comprehensive, 5%–35% business, flat 20% on interest, dividends, rent, property transfer and incidental income); Art. 6(5) property-transfer taxable amount = proceeds less original cost and reasonable expenses; Art. 7 foreign tax credit; Art. 10(5) and Art. 13 (a person cancelling PRC household registration on emigrating must complete a tax settlement before cancellation); Art. 15 (property-transfer tax clearance certificate is checked before registration)."},{"id":"S10","title":"最高人民法院 最高人民检察院 关于办理非法从事资金支付结算业务、非法买卖外汇刑事案件适用法律若干问题的解释, 法释〔2019〕1号","publisher":"Supreme People's Court / Supreme People's Procuratorate, via Hunan Provincial People's Government portal","url":"http://www.hunan.gov.cn/zqt/zcsd/201901/t20190131_13641628.html","tier":"official","checked":"2026-11-07","supports":"Art. 2: buying and selling foreign exchange without authorisation, or disguised trading (变相买卖外汇), that disturbs financial order is prosecuted as illegal business operation under Art. 225(4) of the Criminal Law; Art. 3: 'serious circumstances' at an illegal turnover of RMB 5,000,000 or illegal gains of RMB 100,000; Art. 4: 'especially serious' at RMB 25,000,000 or RMB 500,000; Art. 5: where money laundering is also constituted, the heavier provision applies; Art. 11: FX amounts are converted at the CNY mid-rate on the date of the offence."},{"id":"S11","title":"财政部 税务总局公告2019年第35号 — 非居民个人和无住所居民个人有关个人所得税政策","publisher":"Ministry of Finance / STA, republished by Guizhou Provincial Finance Department","url":"https://czt.guizhou.gov.cn/ztzl/jsjf/201906/t20190614_64883557.html","tier":"official","checked":"2026-11-07","supports":"Source rules for salaries of non-residents (≤90 days, 90–183 days) and the treatment of non-domiciled resident individuals who have been resident for 183+ days in consecutive years; after six consecutive such years without a single absence of more than 30 days, worldwide salary income becomes taxable in China; the six-year count starts from 2019."},{"id":"S12","title":"Report of Foreign Bank and Financial Accounts (FBAR)","publisher":"Internal Revenue Service","url":"https://www.irs.gov/businesses/small-businesses-self-employed/report-of-foreign-bank-and-financial-accounts-fbar","tier":"official","checked":"2026-11-07","supports":"A U.S. person with a financial interest in, or signature authority over, foreign financial accounts whose aggregate value exceeded USD 10,000 at any time in the calendar year must file FinCEN Form 114; whether the account produced taxable income is irrelevant; due 15 April with automatic extension to 15 October; recordkeeping for five years; civil penalty maximums in Title 31 are adjusted annually for inflation."},{"id":"S13","title":"31 CFR 1010.821 — Penalty adjustment and table","publisher":"FinCEN / eCFR (Office of the Federal Register)","url":"https://www.ecfr.gov/current/title-31/subtitle-B/chapter-X/part-1010/subpart-H/section-1010.821","tier":"official","checked":"2026-11-07","supports":"Inflation-adjusted FBAR maximums for penalties assessed on or after 17 January 2025: non-willful violation USD 16,536 (31 U.S.C. 5321(a)(5)(B)(i)); willful violation USD 165,353 (31 U.S.C. 5321(a)(5)(C)(i)(I))."},{"id":"S14","title":"31 U.S.C. § 5321 — Civil penalties","publisher":"U.S. Code (Cornell LII reproduction)","url":"https://www.law.cornell.edu/uscode/text/31/5321","tier":"third-party","checked":"2026-11-07","supports":"Structure of the FBAR penalty in § 5321(a)(5): non-willful capped at USD 10,000 with a reasonable-cause exception; willful raised to the greater of USD 100,000 or 50 percent of the account balance at the time of the violation. Statutory base amounts; the operative current figures are the inflation-adjusted ones in S13. Non-.gov mirror — flagged for review."},{"id":"S15","title":"31 CFR 1010.340 — Reports of transportation of currency or monetary instruments","publisher":"FinCEN / eCFR","url":"https://www.ecfr.gov/current/title-31/subtitle-B/chapter-X/part-1010/subpart-C/section-1010.340","tier":"official","checked":"2026-11-07","supports":"Any person who physically transports, mails or ships currency or monetary instruments exceeding USD 10,000 at one time into or out of the United States must file a report (FinCEN Form 105 / CMIR); also covers a person who causes the transport; transfers through normal banking procedures without physical movement are outside this section."},{"id":"S16","title":"Do I need to file Form 8938, Statement of Specified Foreign Financial Assets?","publisher":"Internal Revenue Service","url":"https://www.irs.gov/businesses/corporations/do-i-need-to-file-form-8938-statement-of-specified-foreign-financial-assets","tier":"official","checked":"2026-11-07","supports":"Reporting thresholds for specified individuals: unmarried living in the US — more than USD 50,000 on the last day of the year or USD 75,000 at any time; married filing jointly in the US — USD 100,000 / USD 150,000; married filing separately in the US — USD 50,000 / USD 75,000; taxpayers living abroad — USD 200,000 / USD 300,000 (single) and USD 400,000 / USD 600,000 (joint). A U.S. citizen is a specified individual."},{"id":"S17","title":"Streamlined filing compliance procedures","publisher":"Internal Revenue Service","url":"https://www.irs.gov/individuals/international-taxpayers/streamlined-filing-compliance-procedures","tier":"official","checked":"2026-11-07","supports":"Available to individual taxpayers who certify non-willful conduct (negligence, inadvertence, mistake, or good-faith misunderstanding); unavailable if the IRS has begun a civil examination or CI investigation; quiet disclosures do not bar use but earlier assessments are not abated; a valid TIN is required."},{"id":"S18","title":"U.S. taxpayers residing in the United States (streamlined domestic offshore procedures)","publisher":"Internal Revenue Service","url":"https://www.irs.gov/individuals/international-taxpayers/us-taxpayers-residing-in-the-united-states","tier":"official","checked":"2026-11-07","supports":"The Title 26 miscellaneous offshore penalty equals 5 percent of the highest aggregate balance/value of the unreported foreign financial assets over the covered period; a compliant taxpayer is then not subject to accuracy-related, information-return or FBAR penalties absent fraud or willfulness; requires amended returns for the most recent 3 years and delinquent FBARs for the most recent 6 years."},{"id":"S19","title":"U.S. taxpayers residing outside the United States (streamlined foreign offshore procedures)","publisher":"Internal Revenue Service","url":"https://www.irs.gov/individuals/international-taxpayers/us-taxpayers-residing-outside-the-united-states","tier":"official","checked":"2026-11-07","supports":"A qualifying taxpayer (non-residency test: no U.S. abode and 330 full days abroad in at least one of the most recent three years) who complies is not subject to failure-to-file, failure-to-pay, accuracy-related, information-return or FBAR penalties, absent fraud or willfulness; no miscellaneous offshore penalty is imposed under these foreign procedures."},{"id":"S20","title":"United States – People's Republic of China Income Tax Convention (1984, with 1986 Protocol)","publisher":"U.S. Department of the Treasury / Internal Revenue Service","url":"https://www.irs.gov/pub/irs-trty/china.pdf","tier":"official","checked":"2026-11-07","supports":"Article 9(2): source-state tax on dividends to a beneficial owner is capped at 10 percent of the gross amount; Article 10(2): source-state tax on interest is capped at 10 percent of the gross amount; contains the standard saving clause (Protocol 1, paragraph 2), so the US may tax its citizens as if the treaty did not exist."},{"id":"S21","title":"Foreign Account Tax Compliance Act — FATCA Agreements and Understandings by Jurisdiction","publisher":"U.S. Department of the Treasury","url":"https://home.treasury.gov/policy-issues/tax-policy/foreign-account-tax-compliance-act","tier":"official","checked":"2026-11-07","supports":"The jurisdiction table lists China as 'Agreement in Substance', Model 1, treated as having an IGA in effect from 30 June 2014 — i.e. not a signed, in-force IGA. Confirms that China is treated as an Model 1 IGA jurisdiction for FATCA purposes while no signed agreement text is linked for China."},{"id":"S22","title":"U.S. citizens and resident aliens abroad","publisher":"Internal Revenue Service","url":"https://www.irs.gov/individuals/international-taxpayers/us-citizens-and-resident-aliens-abroad","tier":"official","checked":"2026-11-07","supports":"A U.S. citizen is subject to tax on worldwide income from all sources and must report all taxable income; FBAR obligation for foreign accounts above the threshold even if no income is produced; Form 3520 is required on receipt of more than USD 100,000 in gifts or bequests from a nonresident alien individual or foreign estate; foreign tax credit and foreign earned income exclusion are available only by filing."},{"id":"S23","title":"Foreign currency and currency exchange rates","publisher":"Internal Revenue Service","url":"https://www.irs.gov/individuals/international-taxpayers/foreign-currency-and-currency-exchange-rates","tier":"official","checked":"2026-11-07","supports":"Amounts reported on a U.S. tax return must be expressed in U.S. dollars; the U.S. dollar is the functional currency for individuals; foreign-currency items are translated at the rate prevailing when received, paid or accrued; the IRS lists Treasury and Federal Reserve rate sources."},{"id":"S24","title":"26 U.S.C. § 988 — Treatment of certain foreign currency transactions","publisher":"U.S. Code (Cornell LII reproduction)","url":"https://www.law.cornell.edu/uscode/text/26/988","tier":"third-party","checked":"2026-11-07","supports":"§ 988(c)(1)(C)(i): disposing of nonfunctional currency is a section 988 transaction; § 988(e)(1)-(2): the section does not apply to an individual's personal transaction, and no gain is recognised on exchange-rate movement from acquisition to disposition — but that exclusion 'shall not apply if the gain which would otherwise be recognized on the transaction exceeds $200'. Non-.gov mirror — flagged for review."},{"id":"S25","title":"《粤港澳大湾区“跨境理财通”业务试点实施细则》问题解答（第一期）","publisher":"People's Bank of China, Guangzhou branch","url":"https://guangzhou.pbc.gov.cn/guangzhou/129196/4332364/4332374/4343888/index.html","tier":"official","checked":"2026-11-07","supports":"Southbound eligibility for mainland investors requires GBA mainland-city household registration (or a qualifying period of local social-insurance/income-tax payment), investment experience and asset/income thresholds; funds move through a closed loop between a remittance account and an investment account; an individual investor quota applies and is set by the regulator."},{"id":"S26","title":"现行有效外汇管理主要法规目录 (Catalogue of currently effective FX regulations), as of 30 June 2026","publisher":"State Administration of Foreign Exchange","url":"https://www.safe.gov.cn/safe/file/file/20260805/d2d0d6ce1441436eadc8bc600eb79c43.pdf","tier":"official-secondary","checked":"2026-11-07","supports":"Confirms that State Council Order No. 532, PBC Order [2006] No. 3, 汇发[2007]1号 and 汇发[2003]102号 were still in the list of currently effective FX regulations as of 30 June 2026."},{"id":"S27","title":"Foreign tax credit","publisher":"Internal Revenue Service","url":"https://www.irs.gov/individuals/international-taxpayers/foreign-tax-credit","tier":"official","checked":"2026-11-07","supports":"The foreign tax credit is claimed on Form 1116 by individuals to reduce U.S. tax on foreign-source income by foreign income tax paid or accrued."}]},"channels":{"meta":{"title":"CNY → USD channels","checked":"2026-11-07","status_legend":{"lawful":"Expressly permitted by an official rule, subject only to documented procedure.","conditional":"Permitted only if the facts fit (specific source of funds, specific applicant status, or specific approval).","prohibited":"Expressly banned; administrative fine and/or confiscation.","criminal":"Can constitute a criminal offence."},"cap_rule":"Where a limit could not be confirmed from an official source it is left blank and marked 'unverified'."},"channels":[{"id":"C01","rank":1,"name":"Emigrant property transfer","name_zh":"移民财产转移","category":"Capital account — approved","status":"lawful","status_label":"Lawful with SAFE approval","applies_to":"A natural person who has emigrated from mainland China to a foreign country (or HK/Macau) and now holds foreign permanent residence or foreign citizenship","best_for":"A large balance that represents lawful property you owned before you emigrated","cap":"No statutory ceiling. Applications up to RMB 500,000 are decided by the local SAFE branch; anything above goes to SAFE headquarters after local review.","cap_verified":true,"requirements":"One single application for the whole amount; written application; applicant information form; business application form; passport plus 中国户籍注销证明 (cancelled PRC household registration) plus embassy-issued or authenticated proof of settlement abroad; proof of the property rights; tax certificate or tax-payment certificate from the competent tax authority; application filed with SAFE where your pre-emigration household registration was located.","pros":["The only personal channel in the rulebook with no fixed amount ceiling — designed for exactly this problem.","Explicitly permits the bank to buy FX and remit abroad (售汇＋汇出) at the approved amount.","Staged remittance is built in: up to 50% first, up to half the remainder after one year, the balance after two years; totals of RMB 200,000 or less can be remitted in one go.","Funds are wired straight to your own overseas account, so the money lands in your name with a clean paper trail for US purposes."],"cons":["You must be able to produce a cancelled-household-registration certificate — if you never held 户口, or the record cannot be located, this route can fail at the first document.","Only property you owned before you obtained emigration status qualifies; assets acquired afterwards do not.","You cannot apply in instalments — one application for the whole amount, even though the payout is staged.","Approval is discretionary; the FX authority refuses applications over property that is legally restricted, subject to litigation, or whose lawful source cannot be shown.","Requires a PRC tax clearance first — and cancelling 户口 itself triggers a pre-cancellation tax settlement under the IIT Law.","Slow: the staged payout alone spans two years."],"timeline":"Approval: no published service standard (unverified). Payout: 50% / +1 yr / +2 yrs unless the total is ≤ RMB 200,000.","verdict":"Primary route for a large balance","sources":["S03","S04","S02"],"note":"Art. 6 and Art. 8–11 of the 2004 Measures; SAFE's own Q&A confirms that only someone who already holds foreign permanent residence or citizenship may apply."},{"id":"C02","rank":2,"name":"Inheritance transfer","name_zh":"继承财产转移","category":"Capital account — approved","status":"lawful","status_label":"Lawful with SAFE approval","applies_to":"A foreign citizen (or HK/Macau/Taiwan resident) who has lawfully inherited assets in mainland China","best_for":"Money that came to you as an inheritance, not as your own savings","cap":"No statutory ceiling; same RMB 500,000 local / above-that headquarters split as emigrant transfer.","cap_verified":true,"requirements":"Single application for the whole inherited estate; notarised proof of inheritance; proof of the deceased's property rights; tax certificate or tax-payment certificate from where the estate was located; passport plus embassy-issued or authenticated proof of settlement abroad; application filed with SAFE where the deceased's household registration was located.","pros":["Separate, purpose-built channel; not limited by the annual facilitation quota.","Inheritance from different deceased persons is applied for separately, so each estate can be handled on its own.","Remittance may be made in one or several tranches once approved."],"cons":["Only works if the funds genuinely are inherited property — your own savings cannot be dressed up as an inheritance.","Notarisation of the inheritance and of the property documents is normally required.","Tax clearance on the estate must be obtained first.","Cash withdrawal is prohibited; funds must go to your own overseas account."],"timeline":"Approval: no published service standard (unverified).","verdict":"Viable only if the money is inherited","sources":["S03","S04"],"note":"Art. 2, Art. 9–11 of the 2004 Measures; SAFE Q&A Q3, Q8, Q11."},{"id":"C03","rank":3,"name":"Non-resident converting lawful current-account RMB income","name_zh":"境外个人经常项目合法人民币收入购汇","category":"Current account — documented","status":"lawful","status_label":"Lawful, documentation-based","applies_to":"境外个人 — a foreign passport holder. This is the category a US citizen falls into under the individual FX rules.","best_for":"Salary, service fees, rent or similar income you earned inside China and still hold in RMB","cap":"No annual quota is imposed on this route — the rules make the annual USD 50,000 total apply to 结汇 and to 境内个人购汇 only. The bank instead checks that the income and the amount are genuine.","cap_verified":true,"requirements":"Valid ID plus documents showing the transaction amount and its source — for income items the rules expressly require tax documents (含税务凭证). The individual FX rules require the bank to verify authenticity and to stop splitting designed to evade limits.","pros":["Not capped by the USD 50,000 annual total, because that total is framed for residents' purchases and for everyone's sales of FX.","Can be repeated per income event, so it is not a one-shot application.","Once the money is in your FX savings account, remitting it abroad needs only your ID.","Comes with a natural paper trail (contract, payslips, tax receipts) that also supports your US filing."],"cons":["Restricted to current-account income — it does not cover capital gains, property sale proceeds or investment returns.","The bank, not you, decides whether the documentation is sufficient; refusals are not appealable in a simple process.","Requires Chinese tax documents, so any untaxed income must be regularised first.","This is the category most often misread: it does not apply if the bank has you on file as a 境内个人."],"timeline":"Same-day to a few days per transaction, subject to bank review (unverified).","verdict":"Best route if the money is China-earned income","sources":["S01","S02","S26"],"note":"Art. 13 of PBC Order [2006] No. 3; Art. 13(1) and Art. 2 of 汇发[2007]1号; Art. 37 of the Measures defines who is 境外个人."},{"id":"C04","rank":4,"name":"Re-conversion of unused RMB against the original exchange memo","name_zh":"原兑换未用完的人民币兑回","category":"Current account — documented","status":"lawful","status_label":"Lawful, documentation-based","applies_to":"境外个人","best_for":"RMB that came from foreign currency you personally exchanged into CNY in the first place","cap":"Limited to the amount of the original exchange; the original exchange memo is valid for 24 months from the exchange date. Same-day exchanges of up to USD 500 equivalent (and up to USD 1,000 at border points before departure) need only ID.","cap_verified":true,"requirements":"Valid ID plus the original exchange memo (原兑换水单) for amounts above the small-value thresholds.","pros":["Mechanically simple: the memo proves the RMB is just your own returned foreign currency, so no new quota is used.","Expressly written into the implementing rules, so front-line bank staff should recognise it.","Converts a stale RMB balance back into the currency it came from."],"cons":["Hard 24-month window from the date of the original exchange — older balances are outside the rule.","Only covers what actually came in as FX; RMB earned inside China does not qualify.","You need the physical or electronic memo; if it is lost this route is closed."],"timeline":"Same day.","verdict":"Fast win if you kept the exchange memos","sources":["S01","S02"],"note":"Art. 15 of PBC Order [2006] No. 3; Art. 13(2) of 汇发[2007]1号."},{"id":"C05","rank":5,"name":"Remitting FX already sitting in a foreign-currency savings account","name_zh":"境外个人外汇储蓄账户汇出境外","category":"Current account — documented","status":"lawful","status_label":"Lawful — ID only","applies_to":"境外个人","best_for":"A balance that is already in USD or another foreign currency rather than RMB","cap":"No amount limit stated for account transfers; cash carried out over USD 10,000 needs extra documents.","cap_verified":true,"requirements":"Valid ID for an outward remittance from an FX savings account. Cash remittances above USD 10,000 equivalent per day additionally require the customs-declared inbound form or the original cash-withdrawal slip.","pros":["The lightest documentation in the whole system — ID only for account-to-account transfers.","No quota is consumed.","Shows that the hard part is the RMB-to-FX conversion, not the outbound wire."],"cons":["Does nothing for a CNY balance — you still need a conversion route first.","Banks still run AML monitoring on the wire."],"timeline":"1–3 business days.","verdict":"Useful only after conversion","sources":["S02"],"note":"Art. 15(1) of 汇发[2007]1号."},{"id":"C06","rank":6,"name":"Proceeds of selling China property owned by a non-resident","name_zh":"境外个人出售境内商品房所得购汇汇出","category":"Capital account — approved","status":"conditional","status_label":"Lawful with SAFE approval","applies_to":"境外个人 who sold residential property in China that they owned for own use","best_for":"Money that is specifically the net proceeds of a China property sale","cap":"No statutory ceiling stated in the rule; the sale must satisfy the self-use principle and the FX rules for the real-estate market.","cap_verified":true,"requirements":"SAFE approval (经外汇局核准) before conversion and remittance; purchase must have complied with the self-use principle; supporting documents are those required by the SAFE/Ministry of Construction real-estate FX notice referenced in the implementing rules.","pros":["Expressly contemplated by Art. 22 of the individual FX measures.","Uses the property-sale tax clearance that you need anyway to register the transfer.","One of the few capital-account exits written specifically for individuals."],"cons":["Requires SAFE approval — a discretionary administrative step, not a bank formality.","Only applies to real-estate proceeds; other capital gains have no equivalent individual route.","The property must have been bought for self-use, consistent with the rules on foreigners buying property.","The underlying gain is taxable in China at 20% before any of this can happen."],"timeline":"Approval: no published service standard (unverified).","verdict":"Viable for property proceeds only","sources":["S01","S02","S09"],"note":"Art. 22 of PBC Order [2006] No. 3; Art. 21 of 汇发[2007]1号 refers to the SAFE/MOC real-estate FX notice. The detail of that notice was not re-verified in this pass — flagged."},{"id":"C07","rank":7,"name":"The USD 50,000 annual facilitation quota","name_zh":"个人年度便利化额度（等值5万美元）","category":"Current account — quota","status":"lawful","status_label":"Lawful, capped","applies_to":"境内个人 for purchases of FX; the annual total for 结汇 applies to all individuals","best_for":"Small amounts, or drip-feeding a balance out over many years","cap":"USD 50,000 equivalent per person per year for 结汇 and for 境内个人购汇 combined with the annual-total framework.","cap_verified":true,"requirements":"Valid ID inside the annual total. Above the total, current-account purposes need genuine supporting documents; capital-account purposes follow the capital-account rules.","pros":["Simple, branch-level, same-day process with no approval file.","Predictable and repeatable every calendar year.","The most widely understood route, so bank staff handle it routinely."],"cons":["USD 50,000 a year means 20 years to move USD 1 million — and the rule has not been raised since 2007.","The quota is per person per year and may not be pooled: splitting across family members to evade the limit is expressly prohibited.","It is a current-account facility; using it to fund overseas property or securities is outside what it authorises.","It applies to 境内个人 purchases — a US citizen classified as 境外个人 is not capped by this figure but instead needs source documents."],"timeline":"Same day at the branch.","verdict":"Only for small amounts","sources":["S02","S01"],"note":"Art. 2 of 汇发[2007]1号; Art. 9 of PBC Order [2006] No. 3."},{"id":"C08","rank":8,"name":"Above-quota current-account purchase with genuine documents","name_zh":"超年度总额经常项目购汇","category":"Current account — documented","status":"conditional","status_label":"Lawful only for a genuine purpose","applies_to":"境内个人","best_for":"Genuine study, medical or travel costs above the annual total","cap":"No fixed cap, but bounded by the documented cost of the underlying transaction.","cap_verified":true,"requirements":"Valid ID plus documents showing the amount of the transaction (tuition, hospital bills, travel bookings, etc.).","pros":["A real way to exceed USD 50,000 for a genuine current-account need.","Documentation is straightforward and verifiable."],"cons":["Strictly purpose-bound — it cannot be repurposed into a general capital exit.","Presenting a false purpose is illegal arbitrage of FX and is fined on the amount involved.","Each transaction needs its own evidence."],"timeline":"Days.","verdict":"Not a wealth-transfer route","sources":["S02","S05"],"note":"Art. 12 of 汇发[2007]1号; Arts. 12 and 40 of the FX Regulations."},{"id":"C09","rank":9,"name":"Resident outbound direct investment (ODI)","name_zh":"境内个人对外直接投资","category":"Capital account — approved","status":"conditional","status_label":"Lawful with approval and registration","applies_to":"境内个人","best_for":"Setting up or capitalising a real business abroad","cap":"No personal amount cap stated in the individual FX rules; approval and overseas investment FX registration are required.","cap_verified":true,"requirements":"SAFE approval to buy FX or use own FX, plus overseas investment FX registration; approval or filing with the competent authorities first where required.","pros":["A legitimate capital-account exit, and the only one for genuinely entrepreneurial money.","Once registered, the investment has a documented basis for future profit repatriation."],"cons":["Not available for moving personal savings — it requires an actual outbound investment project.","Multi-stage approval touching commerce, NDRC and SAFE processes.","Overseas investment also creates US reporting (Forms 5471/8865/926 as applicable) — not covered in this project."],"timeline":"Months.","verdict":"Only for a genuine business","sources":["S02","S05"],"note":"Art. 16 of 汇发[2007]1号; Arts. 17 and 22 of the FX Regulations."},{"id":"C10","rank":10,"name":"QDII funds and bank products","name_zh":"合格境内机构投资者（QDII）","category":"Capital account — collective","status":"conditional","status_label":"Lawful but not a cash-out","applies_to":"境内个人","best_for":"Gaining foreign-currency exposure, not for repatriating cash","cap":"","cap_verified":false,"requirements":"Buy a QDII product through a bank or fund manager that holds the qualification.","pros":["Expressly permitted for residents, so no personal approval file.","Converts RMB into foreign-currency assets inside a regulated wrapper."],"cons":["Your money stays inside the product; redeeming returns RMB to your China account, so it is not an exit.","QDII capacity is rationed and products are sometimes closed to new money.","Adds market risk on top of the currency question."],"timeline":"Product dependent.","verdict":"Does not solve the problem","sources":["S02"],"note":"Art. 17 of 汇发[2007]1号. QDII capacity is set institution by institution; no per-person quota figure was confirmed from an official source, so the cap is left blank."},{"id":"C11","rank":11,"name":"Employee stock ownership / share option plans","name_zh":"境外上市公司员工持股计划、认股期权","category":"Capital account — employment","status":"conditional","status_label":"Lawful with employer-led approval","applies_to":"境内个人 employed by a listed group","best_for":"Share-sale proceeds and dividends from your employer's offshore plan","cap":"No personal cap stated; approval runs through the employer or domestic agent.","cap_verified":true,"requirements":"The employer or domestic agent applies to SAFE for the plan; sale proceeds and dividends are repatriated to a dedicated domestic FX account and may then be converted or moved to your FX savings account.","pros":["A genuine, documented route for equity compensation.","Proceeds can lawfully be converted once repatriated."],"cons":["Only exists if you actually have such a plan and the employer runs the SAFE filing.","The money must come back into China first — it is not a direct offshore exit."],"timeline":"Employer-cycle dependent.","verdict":"Not applicable to a bank balance","sources":["S02"],"note":"Art. 18 of 汇发[2007]1号."},{"id":"C12","rank":12,"name":"Spending on a Chinese card while abroad","name_zh":"银行卡境外消费","category":"Current account — consumption","status":"lawful","status_label":"Lawful for genuine spending","applies_to":"Any holder of a mainland-issued card","best_for":"Paying real expenses — travel, study, online purchases — without touching FX quotas","cap":"Card spending for genuine current-account purposes does not count against the USD 50,000 facilitation quota; the annual RMB 100,000 cap applies to cash withdrawals, not to purchases.","cap_verified":true,"requirements":"A mainland-issued card and a genuine underlying purchase.","pros":["Spends RMB directly at the point of sale, converting at card-scheme rates.","Does not consume the annual quota.","Needs no approval file of any kind."],"cons":["You receive goods or services, not dollars — it does not turn a balance into cash you can invest.","Using cards to extract value artificially (fake transactions, refund loops) is a violation, not a workaround."],"timeline":"Instant.","verdict":"Useful for living costs, not for capital","sources":["S06"],"note":"SAFE Q&A to 汇发[2017]29号, question 3."},{"id":"C13","rank":13,"name":"Overseas ATM cash withdrawals","name_zh":"银行卡境外提取现金","category":"Cash","status":"conditional","status_label":"Lawful within a hard cap","applies_to":"Any holder of a mainland-issued card","best_for":"Small, genuine cash needs abroad","cap":"RMB 100,000 equivalent per natural person per calendar year across all your cards, and RMB 10,000 equivalent per card per day.","cap_verified":true,"requirements":"Your own card. Borrowing or lending cards to get around the cap is prohibited.","pros":["A real, published allowance and mechanically easy.","Useful for day-to-day spending money."],"cons":["RMB 100,000 a year is about USD 14,000 at recent rates — trivial against a large balance.","Exceeding the cap suspends overseas withdrawals for the rest of this year and all of next year, and may be fined.","Cash leaves no paper trail for your US filings and raises CMIR questions above USD 10,000.","Uses the worst FX pricing of any channel (ATM spreads plus fees)."],"timeline":"Instant.","verdict":"Marginal","sources":["S06"],"note":"汇发[2017]29号 items 1–2 as described by SAFE."},{"id":"C14","rank":14,"name":"Carrying foreign cash across the border","name_zh":"携带外币现钞出境","category":"Cash","status":"conditional","status_label":"Lawful only up to USD 10,000 after permits","applies_to":"Any traveller","best_for":"Almost nothing — this is a theoretical route only","cap":"Up to USD 5,000 needs no permit; USD 5,000–10,000 needs a bank-issued 携带证; over USD 10,000 is in principle not allowed and needs a SAFE-issued permit that is reserved for listed special situations.","cap_verified":true,"requirements":"Passport, visa, bank deposit proof or purchase documents, and the permit where required; US-side CMIR filing above USD 10,000.","pros":["No quota is consumed for amounts within the permit limits."],"cons":["The ceiling is USD 10,000 — irrelevant to a meaningful balance.","Taking out more without a permit is punishable with a warning and a fine of up to 20% of the amount, on top of customs action.","Physically risky and instantly reportable on the US side above USD 10,000.","Repeated border runs are exactly the pattern enforcement targets."],"timeline":"Immediate.","verdict":"Do not use at scale","sources":["S07","S05","S15"],"note":"SAFE operations guide citing 汇发[2003]102号; Art. 42 of the FX Regulations; 31 CFR 1010.340 for the US side."},{"id":"C15","rank":15,"name":"Greater Bay Area Wealth Management Connect (跨境理财通)","name_zh":"跨境理财通","category":"Capital account — regional pilot","status":"conditional","status_label":"Lawful but geographically closed","applies_to":"Mainland residents of the nine GBA mainland cities","best_for":"Nothing, unless you are a GBA mainland resident","cap":"","cap_verified":false,"requirements":"GBA mainland household registration (or a qualifying period of local social insurance / income tax), investment experience, and asset or income thresholds; funds run through a closed loop between a remittance account and an investment account.","pros":["A genuine cross-border investment channel with a published rulebook.","Closed-loop design means clean documentation."],"cons":["Requires GBA residency — a US citizen living in the US cannot qualify.","Closed loop: money goes into investments, not into your US bank account.","Individual quota figure left blank and flagged as unverified."],"timeline":"Account opening plus product purchase.","verdict":"Not available to you","sources":["S25"],"note":"Eligibility from the PBOC Guangzhou branch Q&A. An individual investor quota exists but the current figure was not confirmed from an official source, so it is left blank and flagged."},{"id":"C16","rank":16,"name":"Gifting or otherwise transferring property abroad as a resident","name_zh":"境内个人对外捐赠和财产转移","category":"Capital account — approved","status":"conditional","status_label":"Requires SAFE approval; generally closed","applies_to":"境内个人","best_for":"Nothing in practice — listed here because it is often suggested online","cap":"No amount stated; approval is required and discretionary.","cap_verified":true,"requirements":"Must comply with the relevant rules and be approved by SAFE.","pros":["The only textual basis for an outbound gift, and it exists."],"cons":["SAFE's own Q&A says any form of individual property transfer other than emigrant or inheritance transfer falls outside the dedicated measures — so there is no ready procedure for a plain gift.","Approval is discretionary and, for a gift of savings, is not a realistic expectation.","Attempting it without approval is an evasion of exchange control, fined on the amount involved."],"timeline":"Not applicable.","verdict":"Do not rely on this","sources":["S01","S04","S05"],"note":"Art. 20 of PBC Order [2006] No. 3; SAFE Q&A Q1; Art. 39 of the FX Regulations."},{"id":"C17","rank":17,"name":"Returning unused inbound FX by the original route","name_zh":"境外个人未使用的境外汇入外汇原路汇回","category":"Current account — reversal","status":"lawful","status_label":"Lawful — ID only","applies_to":"境外个人","best_for":"Money you wired into China and did not use","cap":"No stated amount limit; it must be the same funds, returned the way they came.","cap_verified":true,"requirements":"Valid ID; the funds must be identifiable as unused inbound FX.","pros":["Very light procedure and no quota consumed.","Statutorily clear."],"cons":["Only reverses an inbound wire; it cannot create a new outbound flow.","Must still be in FX, not converted into RMB."],"timeline":"Days.","verdict":"Narrow but free","sources":["S01"],"note":"Art. 14 of PBC Order [2006] No. 3."},{"id":"C18","rank":20,"name":"Crypto or stablecoin conversion","name_zh":"虚拟货币／稳定币兑换","category":"Prohibited","status":"prohibited","status_label":"Illegal — do not use","applies_to":"Anyone","best_for":"Nothing","cap":"","cap_verified":false,"requirements":"None — the activity itself is banned.","pros":["None that survive contact with the rules. In 2021 this was grey; since 6 February 2026 it is expressly illegal financial activity."],"cons":["RMB-to-virtual-currency conversion and related services are illegal financial activities that are strictly prohibited and suppressed.","Financial institutions may not open accounts, move funds or settle for such activity, so a bank seeing crypto-linked flows will freeze and report.","Investments contrary to public order are void in civil law and the loss falls on the investor.","US side is no better: the IRS treats virtual currency as property, so every trade is a taxable disposition, and an offshore exchange is an FBAR-reportable account."],"timeline":"Not applicable.","verdict":"Do not use","sources":["S08"],"note":"银发〔2026〕42号, section 1(1) and section 6(19), which replaced 银发〔2021〕237号."},{"id":"C19","rank":21,"name":"Underground banks / offsetting pairs (地下钱庄、对敲)","name_zh":"地下钱庄、对敲","category":"Prohibited","status":"criminal","status_label":"Criminal — do not use","applies_to":"Anyone","best_for":"Nothing","cap":"","cap_verified":false,"requirements":"None — the activity is a crime.","pros":["Speed and apparent convenience are the only selling points, and both are illusory."],"cons":["Private or disguised FX trading carries a warning, confiscation of the proceeds and a fine of up to 30% of the amount, rising to 30%–100% where serious.","Where the amount reaches RMB 5,000,000 of turnover or RMB 100,000 of gains, it is prosecuted as illegal business operation under Art. 225(4) of the Criminal Law; RMB 25,000,000 or RMB 500,000 of gains is 'especially serious'.","If money laundering is also made out, the heavier charge applies.","Counterparties routinely abscond or freeze funds, and there is no legal recourse because the contract is unlawful.","US exposure: an unreported offshore account used for this is a willful FBAR fact pattern, where the penalty reaches 50% of the balance."],"timeline":"Not applicable.","verdict":"Do not use","sources":["S05","S10","S13","S14"],"note":"Arts. 45 and 39 of the FX Regulations; 法释〔2019〕1号 Arts. 2–5."},{"id":"C20","rank":22,"name":"Smurfing / 'ants moving house' (蚂蚁搬家) — pooling relatives' quotas","name_zh":"蚂蚁搬家、分拆购汇","category":"Prohibited","status":"prohibited","status_label":"Illegal — do not use","applies_to":"Anyone","best_for":"Nothing","cap":"","cap_verified":false,"requirements":"None — splitting to evade limits is prohibited.","pros":["It is the most commonly recommended workaround online, which is exactly why it is watched."],"cons":["The individual FX measures directly prohibit using splitting (分拆) to evade limit supervision, and prohibit false commercial documents.","Each participant's quota is personal; pooling is evasion of exchange control, fined on the amount involved up to 30% (30%–100% if serious).","Banks' FX systems record every conversion against the individual, so the pattern is visible in aggregate.","It creates a paper trail that both tax authorities can reconstruct, including the relatives' own tax positions."],"timeline":"Not applicable.","verdict":"Do not use","sources":["S01","S05","S06"],"note":"Art. 7 of PBC Order [2006] No. 3; Arts. 39–40 of the FX Regulations; SAFE's card Q&A repeats the no-borrowing rule."},{"id":"C21","rank":23,"name":"False trade or service documents","name_zh":"虚假贸易单证、虚构服务贸易","category":"Prohibited","status":"criminal","status_label":"Criminal — do not use","applies_to":"Anyone","best_for":"Nothing","cap":"","cap_verified":false,"requirements":"None — the activity is illegal.","pros":["None."],"cons":["Using false or invalid transaction documents to buy FX is illegal arbitrage, punished by forced re-conversion and a fine of up to 30% of the amount (30%–100% if serious).","Fabricating payments to obtain settlement is separately criminal as illegal business operation.","The invoicing party is exposed to VAT and invoice offences in China as well as FX penalties.","Once the money is abroad, the US tax return still has to explain the source or it becomes unreported income."],"timeline":"Not applicable.","verdict":"Do not use","sources":["S05","S10"],"note":"Arts. 40 and 48 of the FX Regulations; 法释〔2019〕1号 Art. 1."},{"id":"C22","rank":24,"name":"Hold the RMB and do nothing","name_zh":"继续持有人民币","category":"Baseline","status":"lawful","status_label":"Lawful — the baseline","applies_to":"Anyone","best_for":"Buying time while you assemble documents, or if the balance is small","cap":"No limit.","cap_verified":true,"requirements":"None.","pros":["Zero transaction cost and zero penalty exposure.","The account remains FBAR/8938-reportable, but reporting is cheap compared with penalties for not reporting.","Useful while you gather the household-registration and tax documents the approved routes need."],"cons":["You keep full CNY/USD currency risk on the whole balance.","China has no deposit insurance comparable to the US and account access can be restricted for identity reasons.","It does not stop the clock on US reporting obligations."],"timeline":"Not applicable.","verdict":"A legitimate interim position","sources":["S12","S16"],"note":"Included as the benchmark every other channel is measured against."}]},"taxes":{"meta":{"checked":"2026-11-07","kinds":{"rule":"A rule stated in a statute, regulation, treaty or agency guidance.","analysis":"Reasoning drawn from the rules. Not a quotation. Shown so you can check the logic; flagged for professional review."},"note":"Amounts are left blank where no official source could confirm them. 'Split' means China and the US each tax a different thing."},"items":[{"id":"T01","jurisdiction":"US","kind":"rule","item":"Worldwide income","what_it_means":"Being abroad or holding foreign money changes nothing: a US citizen reports and pays US tax on income from all sources.","amount":"All worldwide income","verified":true,"sources":["S22"],"flag":""},{"id":"T02","jurisdiction":"US","kind":"analysis","item":"Wiring your own money is not itself a taxable event","what_it_means":"US tax attaches to income, not to the movement of your own after-tax principal. No provision in the sources reviewed imposes tax on the remittance as such. What is taxable is the income that created the balance (if not yet taxed) and any foreign-currency gain on conversion (T03).","amount":"0% on principal","verified":false,"sources":["S22","S23"],"flag":"Analysis, not a quoted rule — have a preparer confirm for your facts."},{"id":"T03","jurisdiction":"US","kind":"rule","item":"Foreign-currency gain on the conversion itself","what_it_means":"Disposing of a nonfunctional currency is a section 988 transaction. For an individual's personal transaction, exchange-rate gain is not recognised — unless the gain on that transaction exceeds USD 200, in which case the exclusion does not apply at all.","amount":"USD 200 per transaction (cliff, not an allowance)","verified":true,"sources":["S24"],"flag":"Statute text read from a non-government mirror of 26 U.S.C. § 988 — confirm on uscode.house.gov. The IRS position that a personal-transaction gain over USD 200 is reported as a capital gain was not verified from an official IRS page in this pass."},{"id":"T04","jurisdiction":"US","kind":"rule","item":"FBAR filing threshold","what_it_means":"A US person with a financial interest in, or signature authority over, foreign accounts whose aggregate value exceeded USD 10,000 at any time in the calendar year must file FinCEN Form 114. Whether the account earned anything is irrelevant.","amount":"USD 10,000 aggregate, any time in the year","verified":true,"sources":["S12"],"flag":""},{"id":"T05","jurisdiction":"US","kind":"rule","item":"FBAR penalties","what_it_means":"Inflation-adjusted maximums for penalties assessed on or after 17 January 2025. A willful violation is capped at the greater of the adjusted statutory amount or 50% of the account balance at the time of the violation.","amount":"Non-willful up to USD 16,536 per violation; willful up to USD 165,353 or 50% of the balance","verified":true,"sources":["S13","S14"],"flag":""},{"id":"T06","jurisdiction":"US","kind":"rule","item":"Form 8938 (FATCA) thresholds","what_it_means":"A US citizen is a specified individual. Thresholds depend on filing status and where you live; living abroad raises them sharply.","amount":"Living in the US: USD 50,000 year-end / 75,000 any time (single), 100,000 / 150,000 (joint). Living abroad: 200,000 / 300,000 (single), 400,000 / 600,000 (joint)","verified":true,"sources":["S16"],"flag":""},{"id":"T07","jurisdiction":"US","kind":"rule","item":"Form 8938 penalty","what_it_means":"The statute imposing a penalty for failing to file Form 8938 exists (26 U.S.C. § 6038D), but the exact escalating amount was not confirmed from an official source in this pass.","amount":"","verified":false,"sources":[],"flag":"Unverified — left blank deliberately."},{"id":"T08","jurisdiction":"US","kind":"rule","item":"Form 3520 — large gifts from a foreign person","what_it_means":"Receiving more than USD 100,000 in gifts or bequests from a nonresident alien individual or foreign estate triggers Form 3520. Relevant if a relative in China gifts you money rather than you moving your own.","amount":"More than USD 100,000 in the year","verified":true,"sources":["S22"],"flag":""},{"id":"T09","jurisdiction":"US","kind":"rule","item":"Carrying cash in","what_it_means":"Physically transporting, mailing or shipping more than USD 10,000 at one time into or out of the US requires a report (FinCEN Form 105). Bank wires are outside this rule.","amount":"More than USD 10,000","verified":true,"sources":["S15"],"flag":""},{"id":"T10","jurisdiction":"US","kind":"rule","item":"Streamlined domestic offshore penalty","what_it_means":"If you live in the US and your non-compliance was non-willful, this route replaces information-return and FBAR penalties with a single miscellaneous penalty.","amount":"5% of the highest aggregate balance of the unreported assets","verified":true,"sources":["S18","S17"],"flag":""},{"id":"T11","jurisdiction":"US","kind":"rule","item":"Streamlined foreign offshore penalty","what_it_means":"If you meet the non-residency test (no US abode and 330 full days abroad in at least one of the last three years) and certify non-willful conduct, no miscellaneous offshore penalty is imposed, and failure-to-file, accuracy-related, information-return and FBAR penalties are waived absent fraud or willfulness.","amount":"0% miscellaneous offshore penalty","verified":true,"sources":["S19","S17"],"flag":""},{"id":"T12","jurisdiction":"US","kind":"rule","item":"FATCA status of China","what_it_means":"Treasury lists China as 'Agreement in Substance', Model 1, treated as having an IGA in effect since 30 June 2014. A signed agreement is not linked. Practically: Chinese institutions are treated as FATCA-compliant, and you should assume the account is knowable to the IRS rather than assume it is invisible.","amount":"Model 1 — agreement in substance","verified":true,"sources":["S21"],"flag":"Treasury publishes no per-year exchange statistics for China; the operational reality of reporting is not publicly verifiable."},{"id":"T13","jurisdiction":"US–PRC","kind":"rule","item":"Treaty cap on dividends","what_it_means":"China may tax dividends paid to a US beneficial owner at no more than 10% of the gross amount.","amount":"10% of gross","verified":true,"sources":["S20"],"flag":""},{"id":"T14","jurisdiction":"US–PRC","kind":"rule","item":"Treaty cap on interest","what_it_means":"China may tax interest arising in China and paid to a US beneficial owner at no more than 10% of the gross amount.","amount":"10% of gross","verified":true,"sources":["S20"],"flag":""},{"id":"T15","jurisdiction":"US–PRC","kind":"rule","item":"Saving clause","what_it_means":"The treaty does not stop the US from taxing its own citizens as if the treaty did not exist. So the treaty limits China's tax; it does not limit yours. Relief on the US side comes from the foreign tax credit, not the treaty.","amount":"US may tax citizens regardless","verified":true,"sources":["S20","S27"],"flag":""},{"id":"T16","jurisdiction":"US","kind":"rule","item":"Foreign tax credit","what_it_means":"Individuals claim a credit for foreign income tax paid on foreign-source income, which is how double taxation is actually relieved.","amount":"Credit, claimed on Form 1116","verified":true,"sources":["S27"],"flag":""},{"id":"T17","jurisdiction":"PRC","kind":"rule","item":"IIT rates that could touch the balance","what_it_means":"Comprehensive income 3%–45%; business income 5%–35%; and a flat 20% on interest, dividends, rent, property transfer and incidental income.","amount":"Flat 20% on the categories that matter here","verified":true,"sources":["S09"],"flag":""},{"id":"T18","jurisdiction":"PRC","kind":"rule","item":"Who China taxes","what_it_means":"A non-resident (no domicile and fewer than 183 days in the tax year) is taxed only on China-source income. A US citizen living in the US is a non-resident of China.","amount":"China-source income only for non-residents","verified":true,"sources":["S09"],"flag":""},{"id":"T19","jurisdiction":"PRC","kind":"rule","item":"The six-year rule for foreign individuals","what_it_means":"A non-domiciled individual who has been resident 183+ days for six consecutive years, without a single absence of more than 30 days in any of them, becomes taxable on worldwide salary income from the seventh year. The count starts in 2019.","amount":"Worldwide salary from year 7","verified":true,"sources":["S11"],"flag":"Only bites if you are actually living in China; it does not apply to a non-resident."},{"id":"T20","jurisdiction":"PRC","kind":"rule","item":"Tax settlement before cancelling household registration","what_it_means":"A person who cancels PRC household registration because they are emigrating must complete a tax settlement before the cancellation. That is the sequencing trap: the emigrant transfer route needs the cancellation certificate, and the certificate needs the tax clearance first.","amount":"Settlement required before cancellation","verified":true,"sources":["S09"],"flag":""},{"id":"T21","jurisdiction":"PRC","kind":"rule","item":"Tax on a property sale","what_it_means":"Property-transfer income is taxed at 20% of proceeds less original cost and reasonable expenses, and the registration authority checks the tax-clearance certificate before it will register the transfer.","amount":"20% of the gain","verified":true,"sources":["S09"],"flag":""},{"id":"T22","jurisdiction":"PRC","kind":"rule","item":"Tax clearance before an outward transfer","what_it_means":"The outward property-transfer application must include a tax certificate or tax-payment certificate from the competent tax authority; below RMB 150,000 in total the tax certificate is not demanded.","amount":"Certificate required; waived under RMB 150,000","verified":true,"sources":["S03","S04"],"flag":""},{"id":"T23","jurisdiction":"PRC","kind":"analysis","item":"Converting RMB into USD is not on the list of taxable items","what_it_means":"The IIT Law sets out a closed list of nine income categories. Currency conversion is not one of them, and there is no separate conversion tax. What can be taxed is the underlying income that produced the RMB, and any gain embedded in the asset sold.","amount":"No conversion tax","verified":false,"sources":["S09"],"flag":"Analysis from the statutory list, not an express statement — flagged for review."},{"id":"T24","jurisdiction":"PRC","kind":"rule","item":"Tax on savings-deposit interest","what_it_means":"Interest income is on the 20% list (T17). A temporary exemption for individual savings-deposit interest is widely described, but it was not confirmed from an official source in this pass.","amount":"","verified":false,"sources":[],"flag":"Unverified — left blank deliberately."},{"id":"T25","jurisdiction":"PRC","kind":"analysis","item":"No individual exit tax identified","what_it_means":"The IIT Law's closed list of taxable events contains no deemed-disposal charge on ceasing to be resident; the emigration charge that does exist is the pre-cancellation tax settlement (T20) and the 20% property-transfer tax (T21).","amount":"No exit tax identified","verified":false,"sources":["S09"],"flag":"Analysis of an absence — flagged; confirm with a PRC adviser if the balance is large."}]},"penalties":{"meta":{"checked":"2026-11-07","thesis":"There is no 'conversion tax' in either country. The cost of getting money out of China is the sum of five separate things, and only two of them are taxes. The largest single number on the page is a US reporting penalty, not a Chinese conversion charge.","layers":[{"layer":1,"name":"FX spread and fees","type":"Transaction cost","nature":"Unavoidable, small, and set by your bank","status":"Rates not published by any regulator — see the model below"},{"layer":2,"name":"PRC tax on the source of the money","type":"Tax","nature":"20% flat on property transfer, interest, dividends, rent; 3%–45% on salary","status":"Verified rates; whether it applies depends on what created the balance"},{"layer":3,"name":"US tax on foreign-currency gain","type":"Tax","nature":"Only on a personal-transaction conversion gain above USD 200","status":"Verified statutory text (third-party mirror)"},{"layer":4,"name":"Chinese FX-violation fines","type":"Penalty","nature":"0% if you stay lawful; up to 30%, or 30%–100% if serious, on the amount involved","status":"Verified"},{"layer":5,"name":"US information-reporting penalties","type":"Penalty","nature":"The dominant number: up to 50% of the account balance for a willful FBAR violation","status":"Verified"}],"model_note":"Layer 1 cannot be stated as a number honestly: SAFE publishes no retail spread and every bank's tariff differs. The formula and a calculator are given instead, with every rate left for your own bank's quote."},"penalties":[{"id":"N01","jurisdiction":"PRC","layer":4,"provision":"外汇管理条例 Art. 39 — evasion of exchange control (逃汇)","trigger":"Moving domestic FX or domestic capital out of the country in breach of the rules, including by false means","penalty":"Order to repatriate; fine of up to 30% of the amount evaded; where serious, 30% to 100% of the amount; criminal liability if it constitutes a crime","max_pct":100,"verified":true,"sources":["S05"],"severity":"Severe"},{"id":"N02","jurisdiction":"PRC","layer":4,"provision":"外汇管理条例 Art. 40 — illegal arbitrage of FX (非法套汇)","trigger":"Settling RMB-denominated obligations in FX, or using false or invalid transaction documents to buy FX from a bank","penalty":"Forced re-conversion; fine of up to 30% of the amount; where serious, 30% to 100%; criminal liability if it constitutes a crime","max_pct":100,"verified":true,"sources":["S05"],"severity":"Severe"},{"id":"N03","jurisdiction":"PRC","layer":4,"provision":"外汇管理条例 Art. 45 — private or disguised FX trading / underground banking","trigger":"Buying or selling FX privately, in disguised form, as a dealer, or introducing such trades, where the amount is relatively large","penalty":"Warning, confiscation of illegal gains, fine of up to 30% of the amount; where serious, 30% to 100%; criminal liability if it constitutes a crime","max_pct":100,"verified":true,"sources":["S05"],"severity":"Severe"},{"id":"N04","jurisdiction":"PRC","layer":4,"provision":"外汇管理条例 Art. 42 — unlawful carriage of FX across the border","trigger":"Carrying FX in or out in breach of the cash rules","penalty":"Warning, and a fine of up to 20% of the amount; customs action where a law or regulation so provides","max_pct":20,"verified":true,"sources":["S05","S07"],"severity":"Moderate"},{"id":"N05","jurisdiction":"PRC","layer":4,"provision":"外汇管理条例 Art. 48 — false documents, failure to declare","trigger":"Not filing the balance-of-payments declaration, or submitting invalid or untrue documents, or breaching account/registration rules","penalty":"Order to correct, warning, and for an individual a fine of up to RMB 50,000","max_pct":null,"verified":true,"sources":["S05"],"severity":"Moderate"},{"id":"N06","jurisdiction":"PRC","layer":4,"provision":"Criminal Law Art. 225(4) — illegal business operation, via 法释〔2019〕1号","trigger":"Unlawful FX dealing or disguised FX dealing that disturbs financial order, at RMB 5,000,000 of turnover or RMB 100,000 of illegal gains (RMB 25,000,000 / RMB 500,000 for 'especially serious')","penalty":"Prosecution as a crime; the 2019 interpretation also applies the heavier of the illegal-business and money-laundering provisions where both are made out","max_pct":null,"verified":true,"sources":["S10","S05"],"severity":"Criminal"},{"id":"N07","jurisdiction":"PRC","layer":4,"provision":"个人外汇管理办法 Art. 7 — splitting (分拆) to evade limits","trigger":"Using splitting, or false commercial documents, to get around limit supervision or authenticity checks","penalty":"The prohibition is express; the sanction is the one prescribed by the FX Regulations (N01/N02/N05)","max_pct":null,"verified":true,"sources":["S01","S05"],"severity":"Severe"},{"id":"N08","jurisdiction":"US","layer":5,"provision":"31 U.S.C. 5321(a)(5)(B) — non-willful FBAR violation","trigger":"Failing to file an FBAR when required, without willfulness","penalty":"Up to USD 16,536 per violation (inflation-adjusted, penalties assessed from 17 January 2025); a reasonable-cause exception applies","max_pct":null,"verified":true,"sources":["S13","S14","S12"],"severity":"Moderate"},{"id":"N09","jurisdiction":"US","layer":5,"provision":"31 U.S.C. 5321(a)(5)(C) — willful FBAR violation","trigger":"Willfully failing to file, or willfully causing a violation","penalty":"Up to USD 165,353, or 50% of the balance in the account at the time of the violation, whichever is greater; the reasonable-cause defence is unavailable","max_pct":50,"verified":true,"sources":["S13","S14","S12"],"severity":"Severe"},{"id":"N10","jurisdiction":"US","layer":5,"provision":"26 U.S.C. 6038D — failure to file Form 8938","trigger":"Not filing Form 8938 when the threshold is met","penalty":"","max_pct":null,"verified":false,"sources":[],"severity":"Unverified","flag":"The penalty provision exists; the exact escalating amount was not confirmed from an official source in this pass. Left blank."},{"id":"N11","jurisdiction":"US","layer":5,"provision":"Streamlined domestic offshore penalty","trigger":"Electing the streamlined procedures while living in the US","penalty":"5% of the highest aggregate balance of the unreported assets, in place of information-return and FBAR penalties","max_pct":5,"verified":true,"sources":["S18"],"severity":"Low"},{"id":"N12","jurisdiction":"US","layer":5,"provision":"Streamlined foreign offshore procedures","trigger":"Electing the foreign procedures while meeting the non-residency test","penalty":"No miscellaneous offshore penalty, and no failure-to-file, accuracy-related, information-return or FBAR penalties absent fraud or willfulness","max_pct":0,"verified":true,"sources":["S19"],"severity":"None"},{"id":"N13","jurisdiction":"US","layer":5,"provision":"31 CFR 1010.340 — unreported cross-border currency","trigger":"Physically moving more than USD 10,000 in or out without a FinCEN Form 105","penalty":"","max_pct":null,"verified":false,"sources":["S15"],"severity":"Unverified","flag":"The reporting duty is verified; the specific civil and criminal penalty amounts were not confirmed from an official source in this pass. Left blank."},{"id":"N14","jurisdiction":"PRC","layer":2,"provision":"IIT Law Art. 3(3) — flat rate on the categories that matter","trigger":"Realising interest, dividends, rent, property-transfer or incidental income","penalty":"20% of the taxable amount (property transfer: proceeds less original cost and reasonable expenses)","max_pct":20,"verified":true,"sources":["S09"],"severity":"Tax"},{"id":"N15","jurisdiction":"US","layer":3,"provision":"26 U.S.C. 988(e)(2) — personal-transaction currency gain","trigger":"Converting RMB where the exchange-rate gain on that transaction exceeds USD 200","penalty":"The USD 200 exclusion switches off entirely, so the whole gain is in play","max_pct":null,"verified":true,"sources":["S24"],"severity":"Tax","flag":"Statute read from a non-government mirror — confirm before relying on it."}],"cost_model":{"formula":"Net USD received = (CNY × rate_bank) − outbound wire fee − correspondent/intermediary deductions − receiving bank fee","effective_cost_pct":"((CNY × rate_mid) − net USD received) ÷ (CNY × rate_mid) × 100","components":[{"name":"Bank buying rate vs mid-market rate","typical_source":"Chinese bank's published 现汇买入价 on the day","value":"","verified":false,"flag":"No regulator publishes retail spreads; every bank's tariff differs and changes. Left blank."},{"name":"Outbound telegraphic transfer fee","typical_source":"The remitting bank's published tariff","value":"","verified":false,"flag":"Not published by any regulator. Left blank."},{"name":"Correspondent / intermediary bank deduction","typical_source":"The intermediary bank in the payment chain","value":"","verified":false,"flag":"Not determinable in advance. Left blank."},{"name":"Receiving bank incoming wire fee","typical_source":"Your US bank's schedule of fees","value":"","verified":false,"flag":"Set by your own bank. Left blank."},{"name":"SAFE application cost (approved routes)","typical_source":"Statutory fees, if any","value":"","verified":false,"flag":"No fee schedule found in the sources reviewed. Left blank."}]},"scenarios":{"note":"Worst-case statutory exposure as a percentage of the amount moved, by route. Percentages are from the provisions above; they are not predictions.","rows":[{"route":"C01 Emigrant property transfer","china_penalty_pct":0,"us_penalty_pct":0,"basis":"Lawful route, documents in order","sources":["S03"]},{"route":"C03 Current-account income conversion","china_penalty_pct":0,"us_penalty_pct":0,"basis":"Lawful route, documents in order","sources":["S01"]},{"route":"C07 USD 50,000 annual quota","china_penalty_pct":0,"us_penalty_pct":0,"basis":"Lawful route within the cap","sources":["S02"]},{"route":"C20 Smurfing / pooling quotas","china_penalty_pct":100,"us_penalty_pct":50,"basis":"Art. 39 (30%–100% if serious) plus willful FBAR","sources":["S05","S13"]},{"route":"C19 Underground bank","china_penalty_pct":100,"us_penalty_pct":50,"basis":"Art. 45 (30%–100%) plus willful FBAR; criminal from RMB 5m","sources":["S05","S10","S13"]},{"route":"C21 False trade documents","china_penalty_pct":100,"us_penalty_pct":50,"basis":"Art. 40 plus willful FBAR","sources":["S05","S13"]},{"route":"C18 Crypto / stablecoin","china_penalty_pct":null,"us_penalty_pct":null,"basis":"Illegal financial activity; penalty percentage not fixed by the notice — see flag","sources":["S08"]},{"route":"C13 Overseas ATM cash","china_penalty_pct":100,"us_penalty_pct":null,"basis":"Over-cap withdrawals: suspension plus FX Regulations sanction","sources":["S06","S05"]},{"route":"C14 Carrying cash","china_penalty_pct":20,"us_penalty_pct":null,"basis":"Art. 42 — up to 20% of the amount","sources":["S05","S07"]}]}},"flagged":{"meta":{"checked":"2026-11-07","rule":"Nothing on this page blocks anything. Every item here is either (a) a value that was deliberately left blank because no official source could confirm it, (b) an ambiguity inside the official rules themselves, or (c) a fact only you can confirm. Each carries the source that gets you as far as the sources go.","statuses":{"Unverified":"No official source found. Value left blank. Do not treat as zero.","Partially verified":"Some element is official, another is not.","Needs your facts":"The rule is verified; which rule applies depends on documents only you hold."}},"items":[{"id":"I01","item":"Retail FX spread and wire fees","status":"Unverified","detail":"No regulator publishes retail CNY/USD spreads or telegraphic-transfer tariffs. Every bank's schedule differs and changes. This project therefore shows the formula and a calculator rather than a rate.","impact":"Layer 1 of the cost model is blank by design. Get a written quote from the actual branch.","sources":[]},{"id":"I02","item":"Processing time for a SAFE property-transfer approval","status":"Unverified","detail":"Neither the 2004 Measures nor SAFE's Q&A states a service standard for the RMB 500,000 local / headquarters approval split.","impact":"Timeline planning cannot be sourced. Ask the local SAFE branch for its current turnaround in writing.","sources":["S03","S04"]},{"id":"I03","item":"Are you 境内个人 or 境外个人? The two rulebooks give different answers","status":"Needs your facts","detail":"The individual FX Measures define 境内个人 as a Chinese citizen holding a PRC resident ID, and 境外个人 as a foreign passport holder (Art. 37). The FX Regulations define 境内个人 as Chinese citizens AND foreigners who have resided continuously in China for one year or more (Art. 52). A US citizen who lived in China for years can therefore be classified differently depending on which definition the branch applies. The classification decides whether the USD 50,000 annual purchase cap binds you or whether you instead need source documents under Art. 13.","impact":"This single question changes the answer more than anything else in the project. Ask the branch, in writing, which category your account is registered under.","sources":["S01","S05"]},{"id":"I04","item":"China's FATCA status is an 'agreement in substance', not a signed IGA","status":"Partially verified","detail":"Treasury's jurisdiction table lists China as Agreement in Substance, Model 1, treated as having an IGA in effect since 30 June 2014, with no agreement PDF linked for China. The table entry is official; what Chinese institutions actually report, and when, is not public.","impact":"Do not plan on the account being invisible to the IRS. Plan on it being visible.","sources":["S21"]},{"id":"I05","item":"The USD 200 currency-gain rule is cited from a non-government mirror","status":"Partially verified","detail":"26 U.S.C. § 988(e)(2) was read on a Cornell LII reproduction because uscode.house.gov returned a 'temporary format' error and govinfo paths for the section 404'd. The text is consistent with the statutory language, but it is not the official edition, and the IRS's own statement that a personal-transaction gain above USD 200 is reported as a capital gain was not located on an irs.gov page.","impact":"Treat the USD 200 cliff as probable, not certain. A preparer should confirm on uscode.house.gov before it affects a filing.","sources":["S24"]},{"id":"I06","item":"Form 8938 penalty amount","status":"Unverified","detail":"The penalty exists under 26 U.S.C. § 6038D, but the escalating figure was not confirmed from an official page in reach.","impact":"Left blank in the penalty table. Do not treat as zero.","sources":["S16"]},{"id":"I07","item":"PRC tax on savings-deposit interest","status":"Unverified","detail":"Interest sits in the 20% category in the IIT Law, but a temporary exemption for individual savings-deposit interest is widely described and was not confirmed from an official source in this pass.","impact":"Left blank. Assume interest may be taxable until an adviser confirms the exemption.","sources":["S09"]},{"id":"I08","item":"Wealth Management Connect individual quota","status":"Unverified","detail":"The published PBOC Q&A describes an individual investor quota set by the regulator; the current figure was not confirmed. The scheme was revised after that Q&A.","impact":"Irrelevant to you unless you are a GBA mainland resident — the eligibility gate is the real obstacle.","sources":["S25"]},{"id":"I09","item":"QDII individual limits","status":"Unverified","detail":"QDII capacity is set institution-by-institution; no per-person figure was confirmed from an official source in this pass.","impact":"QDII is not an exit anyway — redemption returns RMB to your China account.","sources":["S02"]},{"id":"I10","item":"Civil and criminal penalties for an unreported FinCEN Form 105","status":"Unverified","detail":"The USD 10,000 reporting duty in 31 CFR 1010.340 is verified; the penalty schedule was not confirmed from an official page in this pass.","impact":"Left blank in the penalty table.","sources":["S15"]},{"id":"I11","item":"Detail of the real-estate FX notice behind property-sale remittances","status":"Partially verified","detail":"Art. 21 of the implementing rules refers to the SAFE / Ministry of Construction notice on FX in the real-estate market, and Art. 22 of the Measures gives SAFE the approval role. The notice itself was not re-verified in this pass, so the document list for a property-sale remittance is not itemised here.","impact":"If your money is property proceeds, get the document checklist from the bank rather than from this site.","sources":["S01","S02"]},{"id":"I12","item":"Whether you hold, or can prove, a cancelled PRC household registration","status":"Needs your facts","detail":"The emigrant transfer route requires a 户籍注销证明 issued by the public security authority plus embassy-issued or authenticated proof of settlement abroad. Without those two documents the route cannot start.","impact":"This is the make-or-break document for the only channel without a fixed ceiling.","sources":["S03","S04"]},{"id":"I13","item":"When the balance was acquired, relative to your emigration","status":"Needs your facts","detail":"Only property owned before you obtained emigration status can go through the emigrant transfer. Money earned or acquired after that has to find another category.","impact":"Splits the balance into an eligible part and a part that needs another route.","sources":["S03","S04"]},{"id":"I14","item":"Which of the two countries is actually taxing you on this balance","status":"Needs your facts","detail":"Everything turns on the character of the money. Salary already taxed in China, a property gain not yet taxed at 20%, an inheritance, or money you personally carried in as FX each map to a different route and a different tax outcome.","impact":"The playbook branches on this; so does the tax total.","sources":["S09","S01"]},{"id":"I15","item":"'No individual exit tax' is an analysis of an absence","status":"Unverified","detail":"The conclusion rests on the IIT Law's closed list of taxable categories containing no deemed-disposal charge. That is a reading, not a quoted prohibition.","impact":"Confirm with a PRC adviser if the balance is large or if you are close to the six-year threshold.","sources":["S09"]},{"id":"I16","item":"The implementing rules page is marked '已修改' (amended)","status":"Partially verified","detail":"The SAFE page for 汇发[2007]1号 carries an amendment note: Art. 9(2) was amended by 汇发[2016]13号 and Art. 39 was repealed by 汇发[2023]8号. No other amendment is enumerated on the page.","impact":"The provisions relied on here (Arts. 2, 12, 13, 15, 17, 20, 30, 31) are not among the noted amendments, but the page does not certify that the list is exhaustive.","sources":["S02"]},{"id":"I17","item":"Crypto penalty percentage is not fixed by the notice","status":"Unverified","detail":"银发〔2026〕42号 declares the activity illegal and refers sanctions to the relevant provisions; it does not state a percentage of the amount.","impact":"Left blank in the scenario table rather than guessed.","sources":["S08"]},{"id":"I18","item":"Repository irregularities found at the start of this work","status":"Unverified","detail":"The repository contained only a 8-byte README with no trailing newline: no licence, no CI, no tests, no data, no Pages configuration, no .gitignore, and no COORDINATION.md despite the brief requiring one. All were created in this pass; the licence question is left to the owner.","impact":"No code existed to audit, so the 'repo review' is an audit of an empty repository plus the new build.","sources":[]}]}};
